  "title": "TPNCP: Fix a possible NULL pointer dereference",
  "description": "If the first data_id parsed from the dat file with g_ascii_strtoll is\ncast to -1, then current_data_id can equal data_id but field be\nNULL. Negative numbers don't really make sense anyway.\n\nThese field registrations should probably use proto_register_prefix.\n(And maybe a wmem_map_t instead of a wmem_array_t for implementing\nspare arrays? And, as already mentioned in comments, runtime\nvalue_string_ext for the big value strings.)\n\nThis prevents Coverity CID 1691679 (hopefully it will convince the\nstatic analysis of that.)\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
